{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And all the peoples of the earth shall see that the name of HaShem is called upon you, and they shall be in fear of you.</b> One who is a servant to one of the officers of the king — his standing is not so great as if he were a servant of the king; for a servant of the king — even the officers and governors who serve the king are afraid of him, because of the king's awe, since that servant is called by the name of the king who is their lord. And this is the meaning and interpretation of this verse: it says, וראו כל עמי הארץ — all the peoples of the earth, who are the portion of the stars and the constellations — כי שם ה׳, that the name of HaShem, who is the Master over them and over their officers, נקרא עליך — is called upon Israel, and that Israel are singled out for the portion of the Master — אז ויראו ממך — then they shall fear the dread of Israel. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: כי שם ה׳ נקרא — Rabbi Eliezer the Great says: these are the tefillin of the head." "<b>And you should be roused</b> here, for the letter שי״ן is inscribed here, which is a halakhah given to Moses at Sinai — and it is as though it said: וראו כל עמי הארץ כי שי״ן עליך ויראו ממך — all the peoples of the earth shall see that a שי״ן is upon you, and they shall fear you. Furthermore, the alphabetic substitution (א\"ת ב\"ש) of the great Name yields the numerical value of שי״ן, and this is the great שי״ן of Shir ha-Shirim. Furthermore, the three hundred days of laying tefillin in the year — subtract the Sabbaths and festivals, which are sixty-five days." "<b>And if</b> you gain further insight into the reason for the שי״ן of tefillin, you will find that the שי״ן alludes to the Shekhinah and to the soul of man. And the שי״ן of the four compartments alludes to the Shekhinah that encompasses and fills all the world and what is beyond the world, and bestows power upon the four living creatures of the Chariot; and the strap that forms the shape of a דל\"ת alludes to the four directions of the world, which are governed through the Shekhinah — above and below as well; and therefore the straps are joined and extend downward. And by this it has been explained that all influx comes to the supernal beings and to the lower beings from the Shekhinah. And from where does the influx come to the Shekhinah? From Wisdom (חכמה) and Understanding (בינה). Go forth and learn that this is so from the formation of man, who was created in wondrous wisdom: for the letter שי״ן is inscribed upon his nose, whose two nostrils correspond to the brain, which is the seat of Wisdom and Understanding. And the significance of this organ, sealed with the letter שי״ן — which is a vessel of reception — is to teach the people knowledge: that so too the Shekhinah receives influx. And likewise you will find the soul, which encompasses the entire body — within it and outside it — and its power and light spread through the four chambers of the brain: the two front chambers contain the faculty of imagination; the middle chamber contains the faculty of thought; the hindmost chamber contains the faculty of retention and memory. And we have grasped from all this that the שי״ן of the four compartments alludes to the Shekhinah and the four holy living creatures, and alludes as well to the soul and the four chambers of the brain. And understand this."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:42.984542021Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}